	(text "CIRCUIT EXPLANATION:\n1.	CD4060 INCREMENTS EVERY ~20-40 SECONDS DEPENDING \n	ON POTENTIOMETER SETTING.\n2. 	DEBUG_LED IS TOGGLED EVERY COUNTER INCREMENT TO \n	DEMONSTRATE FUNCTION.\n3.	Q14 GOES HIGH AFTER 6-11 HOURS.\n4.	CD40106 INVERTS SIGNAL TO GENERATE A FALLING EDGE.\n5	LM555 IN MONOSTABLE MODE GENERATES A 1-SECOND\n	PULSE.\n6.	PULSE TRIGGERS RESET ON CD4060 TO RESET THE TIMER\n	AND HALT THE INPUT DRIVING THE PULSE.\n7.	PULSE ALSO SWITCHES RFPN06LE N-CHANNEL MOSFET TO\n	DRIVE OUTPUT SOLENOID.\n8.	SOLENOID RETRACTS INTERNAL STEEL PIN, RELEASING\n	ACORN TO FALL INTO CUP, WAKING THE USER."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 43.18 176.022 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9b64dd8a-27d5-4956-a9be-5cc0334fea8d")
	)
